SET_DATA_PROFILE: carry the carrier's roaming protocol

build_set_data_profile() sent roaming_pdp_type as a copy of the home protocol.
Stock sends the carrier's own, which is not always the same. Measured against
the capture on identical firmware, frame+0x76:

    ch0xf5 services.telus.com   pdp 2   stock roaming 3   ours 2
    ch0xf5 sos                  pdp 2   stock roaming 3   ours 2
    ch0xf5 ims                  pdp 2   stock roaming 2   ours 2   (agree)

The carrier database already carries the column -- `ims.db` has
`roaming` alongside `protocol`, and the rows say 3 for both of those APNs -- so
the value was there all along and the builder was throwing it away.

The field feeds the profile table the CP matches URSP route selection against,
which is the machinery behind the 2253/168 refusals, so a wrong value there is
not cosmetic.

A new entry point rather than a changed signature: build_set_data_profile()
keeps its meaning for callers that genuinely have one protocol, and forwards to
the new one with the home protocol for both. The FFI gains
samsung_sit_build_set_data_profile_roaming and keeps the old symbol, so nothing
linking against it has to change.

